This project is released under two licenses, because it contains two different
kinds of thing.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. THE DATA AND THE PROSE: CC0 1.0 Universal (public domain dedication)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Applies to:
  public/data/quiz_89R.json         the shipped quiz payload
  public/data/quiz_89R.es.json      its Spanish companion
  i18n/copy.json                    the site's copy, both languages
  data/tx_evidence_vetoes.json      the veto evidence
  and any other data file in this repository

Including the parts of those files that are original work rather than public
record: the plain-language bill descriptions, the why-chosen notes, the outcome
labels, comparisons and caveats, the causal note, the comparator rule, the
computed partisan valences, and the published selection rule.

Full text: https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode

Two notes on what this does and does not cover.

The official bill captions were copied verbatim from the Texas House record and
are not this project's to license. Neither are the roll-call votes or the
chamber totals: they are facts, and in the United States a compilation of facts
carries thin to no copyright (Feist v. Rural Telephone Service, 499 U.S. 340).
They were already free. CC0 is here to remove any doubt about the layer that IS
original, not to claim the layer that never was.

The outcome figures cite third-party sources by name and URL. CC0 covers this
project's description of them. It does not and cannot relicense the underlying
reports.

